            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0689" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-16T20:00:00-05:00">November 16, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>357. Your 920, November 16, 2 p.m. and 922, November 16, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>In the event that the Government removes to Hankow or to a point inland you
                    should follow the Government as far as Hankow. In making your arrangements for
                    this move as well as for leaving members <pb facs="0690" n="683" xml:id="pg683"
                    /> of the staff at Nanking you should insofar as practicable concert your action
                    with that of the diplomatic representatives of other principally interested
                    Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
